Immoral interactions
21.       (1)        Any-
          (a)        male    who    is    found    together    with    one    or     more    female,     not
                     being his wife or mahram; or
          (b)        female      who     is     found     together     with     one     or      more      male      not
                     being her husband or mahram;
          (c)        male or female who is found together with the same gender;

in any secluded place or in a house or room under circumstances which
may                give                rise                to                suspicion                that                they                were                engaged                in                immoral
interaction         or         being         in         physical         proximity         or         any         kind         of         indecent
behaviour shall be guilty under this rule.
“Indecent            behaviour”             may            include,            but            not            limited             to            any            of            the
following acts:
